Promote canary-verified stylesheet repair to HQC production.

Root cause:
- upstream HTML may contain absolute https://homequotecheck.co.uk asset URLs;
- snapshot discovery previously accepted only the AppDeploy upstream origin;
- the production-domain stylesheet reference was therefore preserved in index.html but omitted from the Cloudflare asset bundle;
- Cloudflare SPA fallback returned HTML for the missing CSS path.

Fix:
- snapshot discovery now treats both upstream and configured target origins as local asset references, while still fetching bytes from the upstream source;
- every stylesheet referenced by index.html must be present, non-empty and non-HTML before deployment;
- custom-domain canary run #163 passed snapshot, deployment/domain verification and both mobile quote-intake paths.

Production release must preserve the existing hqc-production custom-domain routing and verify the restored stylesheet after cutover.
